      'Because the oxygen atom pulls the shared electrons towards itself, that end of the molecule carries a slight negative charge, while the hydrogen ends are slightly positive.',
      'As a result, neighbouring water molecules attract one another, which helps to explain why water boils at a surprisingly high temperature for such a small molecule.',
